Yes. The bigger venture is substantially better than “LLM deal finder.”

The useful abstraction is:

> **Given an agentic task, what is the cheapest execution plan that satisfies the required quality, latency, reliability, capability and trust constraints?**

The resource being optimized does **not** have to be an LLM. It can be a model, inference provider, REST endpoint, MCP tool, CLI, hosted agent, GPU, cache, batch endpoint, local model, or eventually another agent on Moltwork.

API Evangelist makes this much more plausible because it exposes 16 years of structured API research, 740+ third-party API services, 400+ open-source tools, governance artifacts, API maturity information and demand-side intelligence covering roughly 5,800 companies—all through REST and MCP. ([API Evangelist][1])

