# 4. `VENT_TOOL_HOTLOADER`

Take Dell's model hotloading concept and apply it to tools.

Don't give an agent:

```text
GitHub MCP
Slack MCP
Postgres MCP
Cloudflare MCP
Stripe MCP
...
```

Give it:

```text
find_tool(task)
```

Oracle retrieves the 3–8 most useful tools.

Then mounts them just-in-time.

```text
task
 ↓
intent embedding
 ↓
capability retrieval
 ↓
candidate tools
 ↓
cost/reliability/security scoring
 ↓
inject minimal schemas
 ↓
execute
```

This is not hypothetical optimization. The recent cloud MCP work specifically identifies context-window consumption and tool-selection overhead as scaling bottlenecks. ([arXiv][2])

**9.7/10.**

And this can eventually become a LiteLLM equivalent for **tools**, rather than models.

