But fallback isn't binary.

You store **behavioral equivalence**:

```text
functional_equivalence = .96
schema_conversion = available
quality_loss = .03
cost_change = -.71
```

Hotloader can therefore say:

> Provider X is rate-limited → swap to Y.

This is how Dell becomes resilient rather than merely cheap.

