Every hour you operate, the database becomes harder to replicate.

That enables things nobody can get from docs:

```text
historical reliability
undocumented limits
promotion history
performance degradation
schema drift
cost/success
free-tier longevity
provider volatility
cross-provider equivalence
quality cliffs
```

**That's the company.**

And the fact that the official MCP ecosystem alone has already reached a scale where researchers tracked **18,966 servers** during an 89-day observation period shows why static catalogs are becoming insufficient. ([arXiv][6])

